hdef jotx mbse_site

  title MBSE Notes
  type page
  description A one-file site about model-based systems engineering: requirements, architecture, safety and testing.

  def menu
    items """Blog | https://mbse.dev
GitHub | https://github.com/balaji-embedcentrum/jotx-open"""

  def tab "Home"
    icon 🏠
    def heading "Model-based systems engineering, in practice"
    def paragraph "Short, practical notes on writing requirements, shaping architecture, analysing safety and proving it all with tests. This whole site is one .jot file: each tab above is a page."
    def gridcard
      layout 3x2
      def card 5i1h7gks
        title Requirements
        icon 📋
        link "#requirements"
      def card zfcradct
        title Architecture
        icon 🧭
        link "#architecture"
      def card gut52mf2
        title Safety
        icon 🛡️
        link "#safety"
    def callout "New here? Start with [Requirements](#requirements): every other activity traces back to them."
    def heading "Latest notes"
      level 2
    def timeline
      events """2026-10-20 | EARS patterns for automotive requirements | done | Five sentence templates that remove ambiguity
2026-10-24 | HARA in an afternoon | done | Severity, exposure and controllability, worked through
2026-10-27 | Tracing tests to safety goals | done | From ASIL to test case in one table
2026-11-10 | Variants without the spreadsheet | planned | Feature models for product lines"""

  def tab "Requirements"
    icon 📋
    def heading "Requirements"
    def paragraph "A requirement states one need, in one sentence, that a test can prove. The pages below cover how to write them, examples, and a review checklist."
    def tab "Patterns"
      def paragraph "EARS (Easy Approach to Requirements Syntax) gives five templates. Pick the one that matches when the requirement applies."
      def table ears "EARS patterns"
        columns Pattern, Template, Example
        rows """Ubiquitous | The <system> shall <response> | The pump shall report its speed.
Event-driven | When <trigger>, the <system> shall <response> | When the door opens, the oven shall switch off its heater.
State-driven | While <state>, the <system> shall <response> | While charging, the vehicle shall prevent driving away.
Unwanted behaviour | If <condition>, then the <system> shall <response> | If the sensor fails, then the controller shall enter safe state.
Optional feature | Where <feature>, the <system> shall <response> | Where heated seats are fitted, the seat shall reach 30 °C in 5 minutes."""
    def tab "Examples"
      def table examples "Requirements for a brake-by-wire pedal"
        columns ID, Requirement, Verified by
        rows """REQ-101 | When the driver presses the pedal, the controller shall request braking within 20 ms. | Timing test on HIL rig
REQ-102 | If both pedal sensors disagree by more than 5 %, then the controller shall use the lower value and set a fault. | Fault injection test
REQ-103 | While the vehicle is stationary, the controller shall hold the brake until the driver accelerates. | Hill-hold test"""
    def tab "Review checklist"
      def checklist
        items """[x] One need per requirement
[x] Uses an EARS pattern
[ ] Has a unique ID
[ ] Has a test or analysis that verifies it
[ ] Traces to a parent need or safety goal"""

  def tab "Architecture"
    icon 🧭
    def heading "Architecture"
    def paragraph "Architecture splits the system into parts with clear interfaces, so each part can be built and verified on its own."
    def mermaid context "System context: brake-by-wire"
      src """flowchart LR
  Pedal[Pedal sensors] --> ECU[Brake controller]
  ECU --> Act[Brake actuators]
  ECU <--> CAN[(Vehicle CAN)]
  CAN <--> ESC[Stability control]"""
    def decision "Two independent pedal sensors"
      status accepted
      date 2026-10-12
      context A single sensor failure must not cause unintended braking or loss of braking (ASIL D).
      decision Fit two sensors with different measuring principles and compare them in the controller.
      consequences More wiring and a plausibility check, but no single point of failure in the pedal path.
    def table interfaces "Interfaces"
      columns From, To, Signal, Cycle
      rows """Pedal sensors | Brake controller | Pedal position (2 channels) | 5 ms
Brake controller | Brake actuators | Clamp force request | 5 ms
Brake controller | Vehicle CAN | Brake status, faults | 20 ms"""

  def tab "Safety"
    icon 🛡️
    def heading "Functional safety"
    def paragraph "ISO 26262 starts with a hazard analysis and risk assessment (HARA), sets safety goals with an ASIL, and then checks failures bottom-up with an FMEA."
    def tab "HARA"
      def paragraph "Each hazardous event is rated for severity (S0–S3), exposure (E0–E4) and controllability (C0–C3). Together they give the ASIL, from QM to D."
      def table hara "Hazard analysis"
        columns Hazardous event, S, E, C, ASIL
        rows """Unintended full braking on the motorway | S3 | E4 | C3 | D
No braking when the driver presses the pedal | S3 | E4 | C3 | D
Brake light does not switch on | S2 | E4 | C2 | B"""
    def tab "Safety goals"
      def list
        listtype numbered
        items """Avoid unintended braking (ASIL D)
Avoid loss of braking on driver demand (ASIL D)
Signal braking to following traffic (ASIL B)"""
    def tab "FMEA"
      def table fmea "Failure modes of the pedal path"
        columns Part, Failure mode, Effect, Detection
        rows """Pedal sensor A | Stuck at full travel | Unintended braking request | Plausibility check against sensor B
Pedal sensor B | Signal lost | Single-channel operation | Missing-signal timeout
Controller | Software hang | No brake request | Watchdog resets to safe state"""

  def tab "Testing"
    icon 🧪
    def heading "Verification and validation"
    def paragraph "The V-model pairs every design level with a test level, so each requirement is proven where it was written."
    def steps "The V-model, right side"
      steps """[x] Unit tests | Each software unit against its detailed design
[x] Integration tests | Units together against the architecture
[ ] System tests | The whole system against the requirements
[ ] Acceptance | The vehicle against the stakeholder needs"""
    def progress "Coverage"
      items """Requirements with a test | 46 | 52
Statement coverage | 91
MC/DC on ASIL D units | 78"""

  def tab "Standards"
    icon 📚
    def heading "Standards at a glance"
    def table standards "Where each standard applies"
      columns Standard, Domain, What it covers
      rows """ISO 26262 | Road vehicles | Functional safety across the lifecycle, rated by ASIL A–D
ISO/SAE 21434 | Road vehicles | Cybersecurity engineering and threat analysis (TARA)
Automotive SPICE | Road vehicles | Process capability of suppliers, levels 0–5
DO-178C | Aircraft | Software assurance, levels A–E
ISO 13485 | Medical devices | Quality management for design and manufacture"""
    def badges
      items """ISO 26262 | 2nd edition | teal
ISO/SAE 21434 | 2021 | violet
ASPICE | 4.0 | blue"""

  def tab "About"
    icon 👋
    def heading "About this site"
    def paragraph "MBSE Notes is an example of a one-file site written in jotx. Open it in VS Code to edit any page, or publish it with jotx site build."
    def button awfj00ue
      label Back to the home page
      link "#home"
      style primary
      align left

  def paragraph
